{
  "message": "**Proposal only — I have not changed any files or database rows.**\n\nThe local demo database currently has 3 active fictional products and 5 offers; it has no digital keys or orders. The existing schema already stores `products.image_url`, and [ProductCard.tsx](/Users/skiut/eneba-homework/frontend/src/components/ui/ProductCard.tsx) already renders that URL in its portrait cover slot. So the image references can use the current schema and card flow; no migration or card rewrite should be needed.\n\n**Image source and rights caveat:** I recommend resolving portrait covers from IGDB’s game-cover records and storing HTTPS image references in `products.image_url` (rather than downloading/copying image files). The source is [IGDB’s image/API documentation](https://api-docs.igdb.com/#images), with image hosting on `images.igdb.com`; its [API page](https://www.igdb.com/api) says it supports commercial projects through a partnership and requests visible attribution for products integrating the API. This is not a blanket grant of each publisher’s artwork rights, so I would show IGDB attribution and treat the result as prototype imagery only unless the project’s commercial use and image rights are confirmed. If that is not acceptable, use publisher-authorized assets instead. I would not use Steam artwork as a shortcut because its [API terms](https://steamcommunity.com/dev/apiterms) include restrictions relevant to presenting Steam data through a third-party marketplace.\n\n**Implementation I propose after approval:**\n- Add 30 actual game product rows with their IGDB cover references, suitable existing categories, and stable slugs.\n- Retire the 3 fictional products from the active catalog and deactivate their 5 offers, preserving rows rather than hard-deleting them so future order/key references are not endangered.\n- Add no invented prices, sales, or key inventory. The 30 new products would therefore show the existing no-active-offers state until real or explicitly demo-labeled offers are added.\n- Add a visible IGDB attribution link. No runtime IGDB API dependency or API credentials would be added to the app.\n\nCandidate titles: Minecraft; Grand Theft Auto V; Red Dead Redemption 2; The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt; Cyberpunk 2077; Elden Ring; Baldur’s Gate 3; Hogwarts Legacy; Helldivers 2; Palworld; Stardew Valley; Terraria; Rust; Dead by Daylight; Resident Evil 4; Monster Hunter Wilds; Forza Horizon 5; Sea of Thieves; Marvel’s Spider-Man Remastered; God of War; Ghost of Tsushima Director’s Cut; Final Fantasy VII Rebirth; Hades; Hollow Knight: Silksong; Black Myth: Wukong; Assassin’s Creed Shadows; Indiana Jones and the Great Circle; Dragon’s Dogma 2; The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim Special Edition; Death Stranding Director’s Cut.\n\nPlease approve or adjust the image source, what to do with the old rows, and whether to keep the new games offer-free. I will wait before implementing.",
